  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676016",
      "title": "How Does User Authentication Work?",
      "lectureOrder": 89,
      "videoOrder": 82,
      "sourceHash": "3f41d2e1ca8efe7d5c81d2d0727096a5458e11b8747265f73f3212959c810c0f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "So how does user authentication work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 7.92,
          "en": "in a Remix driven website?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.92,
          "end": 10.89,
          "en": "Well, in general, it of course works as it works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.89,
          "end": 14.55,
          "en": "on any other website because authentication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.55,
          "end": 18.09,
          "en": "user authentication is a general concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.09,
          "end": 23.09,
          "en": "with various solutions or implementation alternatives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.43,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "In the end, the goal always is that you have a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "and you have your website and that user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "sends their credentials, email and password for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 36.12,
          "en": "and you then wanna validate those credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.12,
          "end": 39.48,
          "en": "in your backend code and grant the user access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.48,
          "end": 43.143,
          "en": "to protected resources if these credentials are valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.16,
          "end": 46.11,
          "en": "Now, one common approach for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.11,
          "end": 49.92,
          "en": "is to validate the credentials and then create and sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.92,
          "end": 51.54,
          "en": "a cookie on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.54,
          "end": 54.54,
          "en": "So in your backend code, sign it with a secret",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.54,
          "end": 58.02,
          "en": "only you know so which is not known by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.02,
          "end": 61.05,
          "en": "And then that session cookie that was generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.05,
          "end": 65.34,
          "en": "can be sent to the user, it then is stored on their machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.34,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "by the browser in a secure way and it can then be attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "to outgoing requests to protected resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "so that then you can check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 78.51,
          "en": "whether a valid cookie is attached to those requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.51,
          "end": 81.63,
          "en": "to the protected resources and only if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.63,
          "end": 84.60300000000001,
          "en": "you grant access to those resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.68,
          "end": 87.96000000000001,
          "en": "So that's the idea behind such a session cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.96000000000001,
          "end": 90.518,
          "en": "you create a session, you create such a cookie,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.518,
          "end": 94.22999999999999,
          "en": "you send it to the user, the user's browser stores it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.22999999999999,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "and then it's attached to requests to protected resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "And in your backend code you therefore need code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "that generates that cookie and signs it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 106.95,
          "en": "But you also need code that validates the cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 109.71000000000001,
          "en": "and checks if a valid cookie is attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 113.55,
          "en": "to those requests for protected resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.55,
          "end": 116.00999999999999,
          "en": "And in this course section you will learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.00999999999999,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "how you can implement all these steps with Remix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 123.33,
          "en": "because Remix, of course is the framework we also use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.33,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "for writing our backend code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "because as you should know by now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "Remix is for the backend and the front end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 133.083,
          "en": "and it seamlessly blends both ends.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
